# Modal/Dialog Patterns

## Summary

This document provides comprehensive patterns and guidelines for implementing modal dialogs in the application. It covers:

- **AppDialog and useAppDialog**: One shared component and hook for **slide**, **drag**, **align**, and **resize** — use these instead of manual Slide/draggable/resizable implementations
- **Standard Dialog Structure**: Basic centered dialogs with Fade transitions, proper accessibility, and RTL support (when not using AppDialog)
- **Form Modal Pattern**: Organizing create/edit forms with logical sections and responsive layouts
- **Memoized RTL Styles**: Performance-optimized RTL-aware styling patterns
- **Loading and Error States**: Handling async operations and validation errors
- **Custom Scrollbar Styling**: Use **ModalScrollBox** for the scroll area and **scrollContainerId** on AppDialog; keep title and actions fixed via paperSx so only the inner scroll area scrolls
- **Scroll Prevention Pattern**: Preventing background scrolling when fixed-position dialogs are open

All patterns include RTL (Right-to-Left) support for Hebrew language, accessibility considerations, and follow Material-UI best practices.

## AppDialog and useAppDialog (slide, drag, align, resize)

**For slide, drag, align, and resize behavior**, use **AppDialog** from `shared/layout-components/modal/AppDialog` and the **useAppDialog** hook from `shared/hooks/useAppDialog`. Do not reimplement Slide transition, draggable title bar, edge alignment, or resize handles manually — AppDialog and useAppDialog provide all of this.

- **AppDialog** is the preferred API: it uses `useAppDialog` internally and renders Dialog, DialogTitle (with DragHandle when `drag` is true), DialogContent, DialogActions, and optional resize handles.
- **Options:** `drag`, `align`, `slide` (defaults: true), `resize` (default: false). Pass `isRTL` and, when `resize` is true, `resizeOptions` (see `UseAppDialogResizeOptions` in `useAppDialog.ts`: `initialWidth`, `initialHeight` / `heightFraction`, `minWidth`, `maxWidth`, `minHeight`, `maxHeight`).
- **Props:** `open`, `onClose`, `title`, `titleIcon?`, `children`, `actions?`, `ariaLabelledBy`, `ariaDescribedBy`, `paperWidth?` (fixed width when not resize, e.g. `"380px"`), `paperMaxHeight?`, `paperSx?`, `scrollContainerId?` (id of the inner scroll container, e.g. ModalScrollBox; when set, AppDialog calls useModalScrollPrevention internally), and any MUI Dialog props.
- **Resize:** When `resize` is true, AppDialog renders three handles (width, height from bottom, height from top). The hook handles top-resize using `rect.top` when bottom-aligned to avoid jump, and the top handle uses an 8–48px skip so the title bar remains draggable.
- **Hook only:** For a custom dialog layout that still needs slide/drag/align/resize logic, use `useAppDialog({ drag, align, slide, resize, isRTL, isOpen, resizeOptions })` and wire `dialogRef`, `handleDragStart`, `resetOnExited`, `slideDirection`, `getPaperPositionSx`, and resize handlers to your own Dialog/Paper/Title. For backward compatibility, `useDragDialog` from `shared/hooks/useDragDialog` re-exports `useAppDialog`; prefer importing `useAppDialog` for new code.

**Example — AppDialog (no resize):**

```typescript
import AppDialog from "@/shared/layout-components/modal/AppDialog";

<AppDialog
    open={isOpen}
    onClose={onClose}
    drag
    align
    slide
    isRTL={isRTL}
    paperWidth="380px"
    paperMaxHeight="90vh"
    title={title}
    titleIcon={<Icon />}
    ariaLabelledBy="my-dialog-title"
    ariaDescribedBy="my-dialog-description"
    actions={<><Button cancel /><Button confirm /></>}
>
    {content}
</AppDialog>
```

**Example — AppDialog with resize:**

```typescript
<AppDialog
    open={isOpen}
    onClose={onClose}
    drag
    align
    slide
    resize
    isRTL={isRTL}
    resizeOptions={{
        initialWidth: 440,
        heightFraction: 0.6,
        minWidth: 360,
        maxWidth: 900,
        minHeight: 300,
    }}
    title={title}
    titleIcon={<Icon />}
    ariaLabelledBy="my-dialog-title"
    ariaDescribedBy="my-dialog-description"
    actions={<><Button cancel /><Button confirm /></>}
>
    {content}
</AppDialog>
```

**Example — useAppDialog for custom dialog:** Use when you need the same behavior (slide, drag, align, resize) but a different structure. Call `useAppDialog({ drag, align, slide, resize, isRTL, isOpen, resizeOptions })`, then use `dialogRef`, `handleDragStart`, `resetOnExited`, `slideDirection`, `getPaperPositionSx(theme, opts)`, and when `resize` is true: `handleResizeWidthStart`, `handleResizeHeightBottomStart`, `handleResizeHeightTopStart` (with the 8–48px skip on top handle). Pass `TransitionProps={{ onExited: resetOnExited }}` and when using Slide, `TransitionProps={{ direction: slideDirection, onExited: resetOnExited }}`.

## 🪟 Modal/Dialog Patterns

### Standard Dialog Structure (centered, no slide/drag/align/resize)

**When you need a simple centered dialog (Fade transition, no drag/align/slide/resize), use this structure. For edge-aligned, draggable, or resizable dialogs, use AppDialog instead (see above).**

```typescript
import { Dialog, DialogTitle, DialogContent, DialogActions, Button, Box, useTheme } from "@mui/material";
import Fade from "@mui/material/Fade";
import { useTranslation } from "react-i18next";

const { t, i18n } = useTranslation(["namespace", "common"]);
const theme = useTheme();
const isRTL = i18n.language === "he";

<Dialog
    open={isOpen}
    onClose={onClose}
    TransitionComponent={Fade as any}
    transitionDuration={{ enter: 300, exit: 200 }}
    maxWidth="sm" // or "md", "lg", "xl"
    fullWidth
    disableEnforceFocus={false}
    disableAutoFocus={false}
    keepMounted
    aria-labelledby="dialog-title"
    aria-describedby="dialog-description"
    PaperProps={{
        elevation: 24,
        role: "dialog",
        "aria-modal": "true",
        dir: isRTL ? "rtl" : "ltr",
        sx: {
            borderRadius: typeof theme.shape.borderRadius === "number" ? theme.shape.borderRadius : 4,
            maxHeight: { xs: "95vh", sm: "90vh" },
            zIndex: 1300,
            direction: isRTL ? "rtl" : "ltr",
            // Remove bottom padding from DialogTitle
            "& > .MuiDialogTitle-root": {
                paddingBottom: "0 !important",
            },
        },
    }}
    sx={{
        "& .MuiBackdrop-root": {
            zIndex: 1299,
        },
    }}
>
    <DialogTitle
        id="dialog-title"
        component="h2"
        aria-label={t("dialog.title")}
        sx={{
            display: "flex",
            alignItems: "center",
            justifyContent: "space-between",
            gap: theme.spacing(1),
            background: `linear-gradient(135deg, ${theme.palette.primary.main} 0%, ${theme.palette.secondary.main} 100%)`,
            color: "white",
            fontSize: { xs: "1rem", sm: "1.25rem" },
            fontWeight: 400,
            textAlign: isRTL ? "right" : "left",
            direction: isRTL ? "rtl" : "ltr",
            // Theme automatically handles RTL-aware padding via [dir='rtl'] selector
            // Theme has: "10px 24px 0px 40px" (desktop) / "10px 20px 0px 40px" (mobile) for LTR
            // Theme automatically swaps to: "10px 40px 0px 24px" / "10px 40px 0px 20px" for RTL
            // No need to override padding unless using custom top padding (see ConfirmResolutionDialog example)
            "& .MuiTypography-root": {
                fontWeight: 400,
            },
            "& .MuiSvgIcon-root": {
                fontSize: { xs: "1.5rem", sm: "1.75rem" },
                color: "white",
            },
        }}
    >
        <Box
            sx={{
                display: "flex",
                alignItems: "center",
                gap: theme.spacing(1),
                flex: 1,
                pb: "10px",
            }}
        >
            <IconComponent aria-hidden="true" />
            {t("dialog.title")}
        </Box>
    </DialogTitle>
    
    <DialogContent
        id="dialog-description"
        sx={{
            "&:first-of-type": {
                paddingTop: theme.spacing(2),
            },
            pl: "40px", // 40px left padding
            direction: isRTL ? "rtl" : "ltr",
        }}
    >
        {/* Content sections */}
    </DialogContent>
    
    <DialogActions
        sx={{
            direction: isRTL ? "rtl" : "ltr",
            gap: theme.spacing(1),
            px: theme.spacing(3),
            pb: theme.spacing(2),
        }}
    >
        <Button
            onClick={onClose}
            variant="outlined"
            fullWidth={false}
            disabled={isLoading}
            sx={{
                px: 2,
                py: 0.75,
                borderRadius: 1,
                color: "text.primary",
                borderColor: "divider",
                mr: isRTL ? 0 : theme.spacing(1),
                ml: isRTL ? theme.spacing(1) : 0,
                "&:hover": {
                    borderColor: "primary.main",
                    backgroundColor: "action.hover",
                },
            }}
        >
            {t("actions.cancel", { ns: "common" })}
        </Button>
        <Button
            onClick={onConfirm}
            variant="contained"
            fullWidth={false}
            disabled={isLoading || !canConfirm}
            sx={{
                direction: isRTL ? "rtl" : "ltr",
                "& .MuiButton-endIcon": {
                    marginLeft: isRTL ? 0 : theme.spacing(1),
                    marginRight: isRTL ? theme.spacing(1) : 0,
                },
            }}
        >
            {t("actions.confirm", { ns: "common" })}
        </Button>
    </DialogActions>
</Dialog>
```

**Key Points:**
- ✅ Always use `Fade` transition with `enter: 300, exit: 200` for centered dialogs
- ✅ Set `elevation: 24` and `zIndex: 1300` for dialog, `1299` for backdrop
- ✅ **DialogTitle**: Theme automatically handles RTL-aware padding
  - Theme has: `padding: "10px 24px 0px 40px"` (desktop) / `"10px 20px 0px 40px"` (mobile) for LTR
  - Theme automatically swaps to: `"10px 40px 0px 24px"` / `"10px 40px 0px 20px"` for RTL via `[dir='rtl']` selector
  - **No need to override padding** - theme handles it automatically when `dir="rtl"` is set on Dialog's PaperProps
  - Theme provides `fontSize: { xs: "1rem", sm: "1.25rem" }` and `fontWeight: 400` - no need to override these
  - **Exception**: If using custom top padding (e.g., `pt: theme.spacing(2)`), override left/right padding with RTL-aware values
- ✅ **DialogTitle background**: Use primary and secondary colors with `background: linear-gradient(135deg, ${theme.palette.primary.main} 0%, ${theme.palette.secondary.main} 100%)` for consistent branding
- ✅ **DialogTitle content**: Wrap icon and text in a `Box` with `pb: "10px"` and use `justifyContent: "space-between"` for layout
- ✅ **DialogContent**: Use `pl: "40px"` for 40px left padding (RTL-aware if needed)
- ✅ **Remove DialogTitle bottom padding**: Add `paddingBottom: "0 !important"` in PaperProps `"& > .MuiDialogTitle-root"` selector
- ✅ Always include `aria-labelledby` and `aria-describedby` for accessibility
- ✅ RTL support: Add `dir` prop to `PaperProps` and use `direction`/`textAlign` on all sections
- ✅ Button styling: Cancel (`variant="outlined"`), Confirm (`variant="contained"`), use `px: 2, py: 0.75` for padding

### Form Modal Pattern

**For create/edit forms, organize content into logical sections:**

```typescript
<form
    onSubmit={(e) => {
        e.preventDefault();
        handleSubmit();
    }}
    dir={isRTL ? "rtl" : "ltr"}
>
    <DialogContent
        sx={{
            direction: isRTL ? "rtl" : "ltr",
        }}
    >
        <Box
            sx={{
                display: "flex",
                flexDirection: "column",
                gap: { xs: 0.75, sm: 1 },
                width: "100%",
                mx: "auto",
                direction: isRTL ? "rtl" : "ltr",
            }}
        >
            {/* Section with header */}
            <Box>
                <Typography variant="subtitle2" sx={{ mb: 0.5, color: "primary.main" }}>
                    {t("sections.status")}
                </Typography>
                <Box sx={{
                    display: "grid",
                    gap: 1,
                    "@media (min-width: 600px)": {
                        gridTemplateColumns: "repeat(2, 1fr)",
                        padding: "8px",
                    },
                    "@media (max-width: 599px)": {
                        gridTemplateColumns: "1fr",
                        padding: "6px",
                    },
                }}>
                    {/* Form fields */}
                </Box>
            </Box>
        </Box>
    </DialogContent>
    
    <DialogActions>
        {/* Buttons - see Standard Dialog Structure */}
    </DialogActions>
</form>
```

**Key Points:**
- ✅ Wrap form in `<form>` tag with `onSubmit` handler and `dir` prop
- ✅ Organize content into logical sections with headers
- ✅ Use responsive grid layout for form fields
- ✅ Use `gap` spacing for consistent spacing
- ✅ Memoize complex styles with `useMemo` for performance

### Memoized RTL Styles

**For reusable RTL-aware styles, use memoization:**

```typescript
const isRTL = i18n.language === "he";

const textFieldSx = useMemo(
    () => ({
        "& .MuiInputBase-input": {
            textAlign: isRTL ? "right" : "left",
            direction: isRTL ? "rtl" : "ltr",
        },
        "& .MuiInputLabel-root": {
            textAlign: isRTL ? "right" : "left",
            direction: isRTL ? "rtl" : "ltr",
        },
    }),
    [isRTL]
);

const tooltipPopperProps = useMemo(
    () => ({
        sx: {
            "& .MuiTooltip-tooltip": {
                direction: isRTL ? "rtl" : "ltr",
                textAlign: isRTL ? "right" : "left",
            },
        },
    }),
    [isRTL]
);
```

**Key Points:**
- ✅ Memoize styles that depend on RTL state
- ✅ Apply `direction` and `textAlign` consistently
- ✅ Use `useMemo` to prevent unnecessary recalculations

### Loading and Error States

**Handle loading states in buttons and content:**

```typescript
// Button loading state: disable during loading
<Button
    type="submit"
    variant="contained"
    disabled={isLoading}
>
    {t("actions.save", { ns: "common" })}
</Button>

// Content loading state
{isLoadingData ? (
    <Box sx={{ display: "flex", justifyContent: "center", py: 2 }}>
        <CircularProgress size={24} />
    </Box>
) : (
    // Content
)}
```

**Display validation and API errors:**

```typescript
// Field-level errors
<TextField
    error={!!errors.fieldName}
    helperText={errors.fieldName || undefined}
    // ... other props
/>

// Section-level errors
{errors.sectionName && (
    <Box sx={{ mb: 1 }}>
        <Typography variant="body2" color="error.main" sx={{ display: "flex", alignItems: "center", gap: 1 }}>
            <InfoIcon color="error" fontSize="small" />
            {errors.sectionName}
        </Typography>
    </Box>
)}

// API error messages
{errorMessage && (
    <Typography variant="body2" sx={{ color: "error.main", mt: 2, direction: isRTL ? "rtl" : "ltr" }}>
        {errorMessage}
    </Typography>
)}
```

**Key Points:**
- ✅ Disable buttons during loading
- ✅ Use `error` and `helperText` props for TextField errors
- ✅ Display section-level errors with error color and icon
- ✅ Always include RTL direction for error messages

### Slide, drag, align, and resize (use AppDialog / useAppDialog)

**Do not implement Slide transition, draggable title bar, edge alignment, or resize handles manually.** Use **AppDialog** (or **useAppDialog** for custom layout) as described in the "AppDialog and useAppDialog" section above.

- **Slide + align:** Use AppDialog with `slide` and `align` (defaults). It uses Slide with `slideDirection` from useAppDialog and positions the paper via `getPaperPositionSx`.
- **Drag:** Use AppDialog with `drag` (default). It wires `handleDragStart` to the title and shows the DragHandle; position is reset on close via `resetOnExited`.
- **Resize:** Use AppDialog with `resize` and `resizeOptions`. The hook and component handle width, height-from-bottom, and height-from-top (with 8–48px skip on top for drag), and reset on `onExited`.
- **Custom layout:** If you need a different Dialog structure, use `useAppDialog({ drag, align, slide, resize, isRTL, isOpen, resizeOptions })` and connect its return values to your Dialog/Paper/Title and optional resize handles. See `shared/hooks/useAppDialog.ts` and `shared/layout-components/modal/AppDialog.tsx` for the canonical implementation.

### Custom Scrollbar Styling

**When the app hides scrollbars globally (`*::-webkit-scrollbar { display: none }`), dialogs with a scrollable area must override that so the scrollbar is visible. Use a dedicated scroll container with an ID and inject a `<style>` tag when the modal is open so the override wins in the cascade. For AppDialog, also keep the title and actions fixed so only the middle content scrolls.**

**Pattern (from UpsertContactModal):**

0. **Fixed header and actions (AppDialog only):** So the scrollbar appears only in the content area and the title/buttons stay fixed, pass `paperSx` that pins the title and actions and makes DialogContent a non-scrolling flex column. The scroll must happen inside a **single inner scroll area** (use **ModalScrollBox** in step 1), not on DialogContent.

```typescript
paperSx={{
    sx: {
        "& > .MuiDialogTitle-root": {
            flexShrink: 0,
        },
        "& > .MuiDialogContent-root": {
            flex: "1 1 auto",
            minHeight: 0,
            overflow: "hidden",
            display: "flex",
            flexDirection: "column",
        },
        "& > .MuiDialogActions-root": {
            flexShrink: 0,
            // optional: backgroundColor, borderTop, etc.
        },
    },
}}
```

**Content wrapper:** The direct child of AppDialog (e.g. a `<form>` or `Box`) must be a flex column that fills DialogContent and constrains the scroll to the inner scroll area: `display: "flex"`, `flexDirection: "column"`, `flex: "1 1 auto"`, `minHeight: 0`, `overflow: "hidden"`. Put **ModalScrollBox** (step 1) as the scrollable child inside this wrapper.

1. **Scroll container and scroll prevention:** Use the shared **ModalScrollBox** component (`shared/layout-components/modal/ModalScrollBox.tsx`) for the scroll area. Pass the same `id` to ModalScrollBox and to AppDialog’s **`scrollContainerId`**; AppDialog will call `useModalScrollPrevention(open, scrollContainerId)` internally so you do not call the hook yourself. ModalScrollBox provides the scrollbar styling (thin, primary-based) and RTL-aware layout.

2. **Scrollbar visibility override (optional):** When the app hides scrollbars globally (`*::-webkit-scrollbar { display: none }`), ModalScrollBox’s `sx` may not win. In that case, in a `useEffect` when the modal is open, create a `<style id="...">` element, append it to `document.body`, and set its `textContent` to CSS that targets the scroll container by ID with `!important`. Remove the style element on cleanup (when the modal closes).

```typescript
useEffect(() => {
    if (!isOpen || typeof document === "undefined") return;
    const trackBg = alpha(theme.palette.primary.main, 0.1);
    const thumbBg = alpha(theme.palette.primary.main, 0.6);
    const thumbHover = theme.palette.primary.main;
    const id = "contact-modal-scrollbar-override";
    let el = document.getElementById(id) as HTMLStyleElement | null;
    if (!el) {
        el = document.createElement("style");
        el.id = id;
        document.body.appendChild(el);
    }
    el.textContent = `
#contact-modal-scroll { scrollbar-width: thin; scrollbar-color: ${thumbBg} ${trackBg}; }
#contact-modal-scroll::-webkit-scrollbar { display: block !important; width: 12px !important; -webkit-appearance: none !important; }
#contact-modal-scroll::-webkit-scrollbar-track { background-color: ${trackBg} !important; border-radius: 6px !important; }
#contact-modal-scroll::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb { background-color: ${thumbBg} !important; border-radius: 6px !important; }
#contact-modal-scroll::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb:hover { background-color: ${thumbHover} !important; }
`;
    return () => {
        const styleEl = document.getElementById(id);
        if (styleEl) styleEl.remove();
    };
}, [isOpen, theme.palette.primary.main]);
```

**ModalScrollBox usage:**

```typescript
<AppDialog
    scrollContainerId="contact-modal-scroll"
    ...
>
    <form style={{ display: "flex", flexDirection: "column", flex: "1 1 auto", minHeight: 0, overflow: "hidden" }}>
        <ModalScrollBox id="contact-modal-scroll" isRTL={isRTL}>
            {/* modal content */}
        </ModalScrollBox>
    </form>
</AppDialog>
```

**Key Points:**
- ✅ **AppDialog:** Pass `scrollContainerId` with the id of the scroll container; use **ModalScrollBox** for the scroll area with the same id.
- ✅ **AppDialog:** Use `paperSx` to set `flexShrink: 0` on title and actions, and `overflow: "hidden"` + flex column on DialogContent, so only the inner scroll area scrolls.
- ✅ **Content wrapper:** Form or Box wrapping the scroll area must have `flex: "1 1 auto"`, `minHeight: 0`, `overflow: "hidden"` so height is constrained and scroll happens only in ModalScrollBox.
- ✅ Use a unique ID on the scroll container (ModalScrollBox) and the same id in AppDialog’s `scrollContainerId`.
- ✅ Reference: `app/[locale]/app/customers/[customerId]/UpsertContactModal.tsx`, `shared/layout-components/modal/ModalScrollBox.tsx`

### Scroll Prevention Pattern

**Prevent background scrolling when dialog is open (for fixed-position dialogs).** When using **AppDialog** with **`scrollContainerId`**, scroll prevention is handled internally; you do not need to call `useModalScrollPrevention` or implement the pattern below. The pattern below applies to custom Dialog implementations that do not use AppDialog.

```typescript
useEffect(() => {
    if (isOpen) {
        // Save current scroll position
        const scrollY = window.scrollY;
        const originalStyle = window.getComputedStyle(document.body).overflow;
        const originalOverflowY = window.getComputedStyle(document.body).overflowY;
        const originalPosition = window.getComputedStyle(document.body).position;
        
        // Lock body scroll
        document.body.style.overflow = "hidden";
        document.body.style.overflowY = "hidden";
        document.body.style.position = "fixed";
        document.body.style.top = `-${scrollY}px`;
        document.body.style.width = "100%";
        document.documentElement.style.overflow = "hidden";
        
        // Prevent scroll events from propagating to body when over dialog
        const handleWheel = (e: WheelEvent) => {
            const dialog = document.querySelector('[role="dialog"]') as HTMLElement;
            if (!dialog) return;
            
            const target = e.target as HTMLElement;
            const isInsideDialog = dialog.contains(target);
            
            if (isInsideDialog) {
                // Identify scrollable elements by ID (e.g., id="dialog-column-list")
                const scrollableContainer = document.getElementById('dialog-column-list');
                const isTargetScrollable = target.id === 'dialog-column-list';
                
                // Traverse up DOM tree to find scrollable container
                let isInsideScrollable = isTargetScrollable;
                if (!isInsideScrollable && target.parentElement) {
                    let currentElement: HTMLElement | null = target.parentElement;
                    while (currentElement && currentElement !== dialog) {
                        if (currentElement.id === 'dialog-column-list') {
                            isInsideScrollable = true;
                            break;
                        }
                        currentElement = currentElement.parentElement;
                    }
                }
                
                // Handle scrollable container
                if (isInsideScrollable && scrollableContainer) {
                    const canScroll = scrollableContainer.scrollHeight > scrollableContainer.clientHeight;
                    const isAtTop = scrollableContainer.scrollTop <= 0;
                    const isAtBottom = scrollableContainer.scrollTop >= scrollableContainer.scrollHeight - scrollableContainer.clientHeight - 1;
                    
                    // Only prevent if at boundary
                    if ((e.deltaY < 0 && isAtTop) || (e.deltaY > 0 && isAtBottom)) {
                        e.preventDefault();
                        e.stopPropagation();
                    } else if (!canScroll) {
                        e.preventDefault();
                        e.stopPropagation();
                    }
                } else {
                    // Check dialog content scrolling
                    const dialogContent = document.getElementById('dialog-description');
                    if (dialogContent && dialogContent.contains(target)) {
                        const canScroll = dialogContent.scrollHeight > dialogContent.clientHeight;
                        if (canScroll) {
                            const isAtTop = dialogContent.scrollTop <= 0;
                            const isAtBottom = dialogContent.scrollTop >= dialogContent.scrollHeight - dialogContent.clientHeight - 1;
                            if ((e.deltaY < 0 && isAtTop) || (e.deltaY > 0 && isAtBottom)) {
                                e.preventDefault();
                                e.stopPropagation();
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            } else {
                // Always prevent scrolling on backdrop
                e.preventDefault();
                e.stopPropagation();
            }
        };
        
        const handleBackdropWheel = (e: WheelEvent) => {
            e.preventDefault();
            e.stopPropagation();
        };
        
        window.addEventListener('wheel', handleWheel, { passive: false, capture: true });
        const backdrop = document.querySelector('.MuiBackdrop-root');
        if (backdrop) {
            backdrop.addEventListener('wheel', handleBackdropWheel, { passive: false });
        }
        
        // Cleanup
        return () => {
            document.body.style.overflow = originalStyle;
            document.body.style.overflowY = originalOverflowY;
            document.body.style.position = originalPosition;
            document.body.style.width = "";
            document.documentElement.style.overflow = "";
            
            if (originalPosition === 'static' || originalPosition === '') {
                window.scrollTo(0, scrollY);
            }
            
            window.removeEventListener('wheel', handleWheel, { capture: true });
            if (backdrop) {
                backdrop.removeEventListener('wheel', handleBackdropWheel);
            }
        };
    }
}, [isOpen]);
```

**Key Points:**
- ✅ Save scroll position before locking body
- ✅ Lock body with `position: "fixed"` and `top: -${scrollY}px`
- ✅ Prevent scroll on both `document.body` and `document.documentElement`
- ✅ **Identify scrollable elements by ID** - Add unique IDs to scrollable containers
- ✅ **Traverse up DOM tree** - If target is not the container, traverse up to find it
- ✅ **Only prevent scrolling at boundaries** - Check `isAtTop` and `isAtBottom` before preventing
- ✅ Always prevent scrolling on backdrop
- ✅ Restore scroll position and styles on cleanup
- ✅ Use `{ passive: false, capture: true }` for wheel event listeners

### Common Mistakes to Avoid

- ❌ **Don't reimplement slide/drag/align/resize** — use AppDialog or useAppDialog from `shared/layout-components/modal/AppDialog` and `shared/hooks/useAppDialog.ts`
- ❌ **Don't override DialogTitle padding unnecessarily** - Theme automatically handles RTL-aware padding when `dir="rtl"` is set on Dialog's PaperProps
- ❌ **Don't add marginLeft/marginRight to the DialogTitle content Box** (icon+text) in draggable dialogs — the theme's padding handles spacing from the DragHandle; extra margin creates inconsistent spacing
- ❌ Don't override DialogTitle fontSize/fontWeight - theme provides defaults
- ❌ Don't forget RTL support - always include `direction`, `textAlign`, and `dir` prop on `PaperProps` (theme uses this for automatic padding)
- ❌ Don't use inline styles - use `sx` prop or memoized styles
- ❌ Don't skip accessibility - always include `aria-labelledby` and `aria-describedby`
- ❌ Don't forget loading states - disable buttons and show spinners
- ❌ Don't use wrong transition - use `Fade` for centered dialogs, `Slide` for edge-aligned (AppDialog does this via `slide` prop)
- ❌ Don't forget `minHeight: 0` on flex scrollable content for proper scrolling

